From 9bd9fcbd848ddfcaae8b123798cb291cba5bee7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:29:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sim): cut the stock along the travelled part of the move
 in flight during playback

Playback showed the voxel stock cut only at the end of each G1/G2 move.
The move under the playhead is now cut from its start to the tool's
drawn position (lines and arcs, via the timeline's own point_along),
on a copy of the completed-move stock: the kept stock, checkpoints,
verdicts and the post are unchanged, and the end of a move is the
plain seek bit for bit. Rotary and turning ops keep whole-move display.

Fixes #1516

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
